  "joint_algebra": "For a weighted normalized KellerF,any coefficient K-algebraA,and direction matrixV,putq_j=(WV_j)^T JF^-T p. The entire zero-constant algebraA[q]^+ is pure-null. It is wholly safe iff every constant K-linear combination is safe iff the formal inverseg(Vt) is polynomial iff the finite joint residual idealJ_B(V) has nilpotent image. Finite momentum-source jets include every source marker. A joint inverse degreee gives commonC(e)=max(e,(2n-1)(1+e*max(H0-1,0)));a polynomialH of origin ordernu has cutoffnu*m>C(e)degQ. This classifies the whole algebra,not individual nonlinear members of a jointly failing algebra.",
  "joint_gate": "For b_N=total-degreeN truncation ofg(Vt),finite coefficients ofF(b_N)-Vt generate exactly the full ordinary joint inverse-tail ideal. The field degree bound isB=D^(n-1),by generic-line restriction;the all-ring functor is formal completion alongJ_B. A nilpotence exponentL gives branch boundE_L=B*((n-1)(D-1)+D)^ceil(log2L) by finite Newton correction andJ_(E_L) subsetJ_B^L. A gridG^r with|G|=DB+1 tests joint safety through finitely many scalar line phases;ordinary Vandermonde interpolation retains nilpotents. Frame changes inGL_r preserve the ordinary ideals,so field safe-subspace equations are basis independent on free charts. No large grid enumerated.",
  "nonclosure": "In the existing six-dimensional map,S=Y1 andT=-Y2 have degrees12/10,all positive joint moments zero,and each has sharp individual coefficient2 by Euler charges-1/+1 and exact witnessesL[p3S^2]=-15,L[zT^2]=-8. Their sum is the earlier unsafe phase,and the pure-null productST of degree22 satisfiesL[xy(ST)^m]=(2m)!/2^m for allm>=1. Safe polynomials are therefore neither additive nor multiplicatively closed,even in a jointly pure-null algebra. Over every coefficient algebra,lambdaS+muT is safe iff lambda*mu is nilpotent;powerL gives sufficient cutoffm>2degQ+2L-2,or common slope2L. Individual mixed nonlinear phases such asS(1+ST) remain safe by charge,so joint-algebra failure is not an individual classification.",
  "product_thickness": "For the degree22 product failureR0=ST,all linear-marker moments vanish by its charge0 and nonzero charges on every source variable,while the fixed degree2 markerxy has nonzero moments at every index. Thus full ordinary scaling-line ideals areI_N=(e^(2N+1)) for each integerN>=0. Parametereta*R0 is safe exactly for nilpotenteta;exact nilpotence orderL gives sharp real coefficient(L-1)/2 and least integer coefficientfloor(L/2). The completion isK[[e]],with different individual levels from the retained linear-witness scaling ideals(e^(N+1)). Standard Gaussian realization uses the same fixed complex linear change,without a smaller endpoint claim.",
